  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "The docs are served at https://docs.devias.io. Every path in these docs is relative to that root: /llms.txt is https://docs.devias.io/llms.txt.",
      "Devias is an open-source platform that works as an operating system for a business: a core (records, views, workflows, agents, permissions) with installable modules.",
      "Pages are typed by folder. concepts/ explains what things are, guides/ gives procedures, reference/ is exhaustive (SDK, CLI, HTTP API), operate/ covers hosting. Use /start/glossary for exact terms.",
      "Every id in a module (module, object, field, view, action, workflow, step, connection, variable, event, policy) is a uuid. Generate them with `devias id <count>`. Never invent dotted or readable ids.",
      "Run `devias plan` and read its output before `devias apply`. Apply only what the plan says.",
      "The OpenAPI document, including the routes of the modules in the reference setup, is at /reference/api/openapi.json.",
      "Devias is young and changes quickly. If a page and the source repository (github.com/devias-io/devias) disagree, the repository is right."
    ]
  }
}
